libtmux-easy (0.6.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Breaking: libtmux_easy.processes.Processes is now ProcessGroup, so it
    isn't confused with the pytest Processes. The old name is gone.
  * Needs libtmux 0.30 or later; the shims for older versions are gone
    (DeprecatedError is no longer exported).
  * lte-run is its own package, lte_run (with the /proc helpers, formerly
    libtmux_easy.proc and libtmux_easy.wrap), so libtmux_easy's __init__
    imports its names directly. libtmux_easy._tmux is now tmuxcmd.
  * Every function has a docstring; Processes' arguments are each
    documented.
  * Processes(env=): variables for every process of a group, under
    start(env=); never os.environ. build() panes and adopt()'s script too.
  * Shell and wrap panes no longer write ~/.bash_history:
    create(history=True) to keep it.
  * The pytest plugin's log directories are TestFoo_0, not TestFoo0.
  * Fix wait_for() and wait_for_output() missing a line printed right after
    a watch began on a pane with scrollback (tmux mode, a fast shell).

 -- Spencer Diehl <docdiehl@gmail.com>  Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:57:08 -0800

libtmux-easy (0.5.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Processes(sigterm_timeout=) and start(sigterm_timeout=): seconds SIGTERM
    gets before SIGKILL, per group or per process (default 5, as before).

 -- Spencer Diehl <docdiehl@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0800

libtmux-easy (0.4.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * libtmux_easy.processes.Processes: the process group without pytest
    (testing.Processes is now a subclass), raising ProcessFailure.
  * close() stops every process in parallel; kill_all() for a second Ctrl-C.
  * on_exit(name, status, died) callback; start(env=, sigint_timeout=);
    prefix="" for bare tmux window names.

 -- Spencer Diehl <docdiehl@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:16:10 -0800

